---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import metadata from '../generated/article-meta.json';
import systemOne from '../generated/system-one/article-meta.json';
---
<BaseLayout title="Praneeth Paikray" description="Notes and experiments on building AI systems. Praneeth Paikray, AI Solutions Architect at Databricks, based in Bengaluru.">
  <div class="home container">
    <section aria-labelledby="intro-title">
      <h1 id="intro-title">Hi, I’m Praneeth.</h1>
      <div class="intro">
        <p>I’m an AI Solutions Architect at Databricks, based in Bengaluru. I work on agent systems, evaluation, and the engineering that helps AI work reliably in practice.</p>
        <p>Here I share experiments, code, and explanations of what the results tell us. My current interests include agent memory, domain-specific agents, and learning from evaluation feedback.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-links"><a href="https://github.com/Praneeth16">GitHub ↗</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/praneeth-paikray/">LinkedIn ↗</a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="writing-list" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
      <p class="section-label" id="writing-title">Writing</p>
      <a class="post-link" href="/blog/how-llms-are-built/">
        <h2>How a language model is made</h2>
        <p>An illustrated field guide to the work before the first answer. Operate an attention head, take a gradient step, and follow a model from text to inference.</p>
        <span class="meta">1 Nov 2026 · 18 min read · Interactive visual story</span>
      </a>
      <a class="post-link" href="/blog/databricks-for-agents/">
        <h2>Databricks Is Databricks for Agents</h2>
        <p>Build and run agents with governed context, agent execution, MLflow, AIR with NVIDIA, and open-model serving. Explore the platform and how its capabilities connect.</p>
        <span class="meta">31 Oct 2026 · 15 min read · Interactive essay</span>
      </a>
      <a class="post-link" href="/blog/genrec/">
        <h2>Reading Tastes, Ranking Titles</h2>
        <p>How language models became recommenders, and what Netflix’s GenRec changes. Explore catalog scoring, training, cost, and the research lineage.</p>
        <span class="meta">2 Oct 2026 · 12 min read · Interactive essay</span>
      </a>
      <a class="post-link" href="/blog/wtf-is-a-system-one-model/">
        <h2>WTF Is a System One Model?</h2>
        <p>{systemOne.subtitle}</p>
        <span class="meta">26 Sep 2026 · {systemOne.readingMinutes} min read · Benchmark</span>
      </a>
      <a class="post-link" href="/blog/adapting-jev-with-gepa/">
        <h2>Adapting Jev to Your Domain with GEPA</h2>
        <p>{metadata.subtitle}</p>
        <span class="meta">20 Sep 2026 · {metadata.readingMinutes} min read · Interactive study</span>
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
